cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this note, code or data, please cite it as below."
title: "Small maximal k-consecutive sums on a circle and the clock-face problem"
authors:
  - family-names: "Nagib"
    given-names: "Victor Nidal Bassem"
date-released: 2026-10-30
version: "1.0.0"
url: "https://github.com/victornagib2/clockface-ksums"
repository-code: "https://github.com/victornagib2/clockface-ksums"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - OEIS A066385
  - clock-face problem
  - circular permutations
  - consecutive sums
  - combinatorics
abstract: >-
  For odd k and odd m, the smallest possible maximal sum of k consecutive entries of a circular arrangement of
  1..mk exceeds the average by exactly 1 when m <= k+2 and by exactly 2 when m >= k+4. The lower bound is a
  total-variation argument valid for all n; the upper bound is an explicit construction. For k = 3 this gives a
  self-contained proof that the clock-face numbers (OEIS A066385) equal ceiling(3n/2)+3 for all n >= 4 except
  n = 5, 6, 9, 15.
